/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-fable-ws/ADJUDICATION-fable-2026-09-10.md:101:- **Training rows are built on the reference carrier's own trajectory.** `run_v025_pilot_c3.py:544-546`: `base = ENGINE._base_configuration(tape, step_index, carrier)`; `incumbent = ENGINE._base_configuration(tape, step_index - 1, carrier)`. The corpus loop `:989-990` is `for step_index in range(30): for carrier in ENGINE.REFERENCE_CARRIERS`. Every feature (occupancy excluding focal, beam/satellite active, previous served association, previous load) and every label `d_i = F(a_i, a⁰_{-i}) - F(a⁰)` is computed with `a⁰` = the geometry-only carrier and `b⁻` = the carrier's previous step. The carrier regime is the one where the corrected rule serves `1,165/2,000` and the sealed rule `826/2,000` user-anchors (`RESEEDED-SPAN` served table) and where the feature census shows a mean SINR margin of `-64.9 dB` with SD `97.8` and a `1e6` infeasibility sentinel on a tenth of rows (`PREFLIGHT-DATA-CENSUS:79-80`).
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-fable-ws/ADJUDICATION-fable-2026-09-10.md:102:- **At deployment the heads act around their own proposal.** `run_c3_panel_smoke.py:330-410`: the proposal is the per-user argmax of the learned Q1+Q2; the catalogue is built around that seed (`_catalogue_with_census(tape, 0, seed, …)`); every row is scored relative to the seed (`_score(model, built, seed, row, …)`). The seed is `+400%` from the carrier (`smoke.json` `FULL - BASELINE = 4.017`); at the fixed point the corrected rule serves `2,000/2,000`.
