/home/sat/mcrl-v025-arch-ws/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTINGENCY-LADDER-AMENDMENT-1-R7-2026-09-08.md:3:**R7 added (exploratory, never primary):** rate target r* = 25 Mbit/s, ordered after R6 with the same 13 arms and certificates. Motivation recorded honestly: the synthetic mechanism map R1 (ceiling arms valid) showed availability ≈ 0.42 with ≈ 40 % unserved under the rate-target architectures on synthetic worlds; the first-principles review notes that the balancing lever weakens at low spectral efficiency; the development smoke on the quarantined world also showed availability 0.59–0.76 at 50 Mbit/s. The primary remains a-r0 at 50 Mbit/s; no primary constant, order, margin or rule changes.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-arch-ws/.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-controller-handoff-20260907/CONTROLLER-REFERENCE-DESIGN-NORMAL-POWER-EE-2026-09-08.md:9:4. **Rate.** ACM maps SINR to a spectral efficiency SE(SINR) from a MODCOD table (DVB-S2X or NR NTN MCS), bounded above by SE_max (≈ 5–6 bit/s/Hz) and below by the lowest MODCOD threshold SINR_min; Shannon-with-gap-and-cap is an acceptable smooth surrogate. Users in a beam share W by TDM (time fractions f_u, Σ f_u ≤ 1) or FDM; equal share is the usual baseline. Per-user rate R_u = f_u·W·SE(SINR_u). Rate follows geometry **every step**; staying on a degrading beam loses bits, not energy.
