/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-PROVISIONING-FIX-2026-09-10.md:23:One consequence to keep visible: at occupancy one the corrected rule delivers 1.362 times the rate target, because the bottom rung's spectral efficiency exceeds what was required. Over-delivery is credited by the current numerator. Whether that is the right numerator is a separate open question, currently under adversarial review.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-TERMINOLOGY-2026-09-10.md:22:**The mechanism — why interaction exists here.** **Inter-user coupling**, and it has two concrete sources in this system: equal-airtime sharing inside a beam, where one more occupant raises the required spectral efficiency for *everyone* in that beam; and co-channel interference between beams through the cross-gain matrix. The solver is literally a **coupled power fixed point**. This name is better than "coordination" because it names the cause rather than the response.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-arch-ws/.scratch/occupancy-convexity/map.md:13:- Production directly defines required spectral efficiency as `eta_req(n) = r* n / B` and chooses modes with `eta_mode >= eta_req` (`src/mcrl/physics_v025/acm.py:77-101`). With the sealed constants, `eta_req(n) = 0.3 n bit/s/Hz` (subject only to ordinary binary64 representation).
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-arch-ws/.scratch/occupancy-convexity/map.md:23:- Maximum table spectral efficiency: 32APSK 9/10 has raw efficiency 4.453027 and ideal threshold 16.05 dB (`src/mcrl/physics_v025/constants_v025.py:118-123`), hence `eta_max=3.710855833333333 bit/s/Hz` and threshold `16.958187539523752 dB` (`49.63851196075088` linear). Since `eta_req=0.3n`, `n=12` remains table-feasible and `n=13` is the first occupancy exceeding the maximum. When no row exists, `rate_target_sinr` returns `None` (`src/mcrl/physics_v025/acm.py:104-118`), and a-r explicitly forces that user's chain to the cap (`src/mcrl/physics_v025/architectures.py:628-645`, `src/mcrl/physics_v025/architectures.py:680-694`).
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-arch-ws/OCCUPANCY-CONVEXITY-2026-09-10.md:15:The TDM scheduler gives each of n beam members one equal 1/n interval ([architectures.py:268](src/mcrl/physics_v025/architectures.py#L268), [architectures.py:278](src/mcrl/physics_v025/architectures.py#L278)). Therefore required spectral efficiency is exactly `eta_req(n)=r*n/B=0.3n bit/s/Hz`, which production computes directly before choosing the lowest-threshold qualifying mode ([acm.py:77](src/mcrl/physics_v025/acm.py#L77), [acm.py:95](src/mcrl/physics_v025/acm.py#L95)). The rate endpoint sums full-band ACM rate over those slot fractions ([architectures.py:245](src/mcrl/physics_v025/architectures.py#L245)); hence this report's pooled numerator is actual delivered ACM capacity, not target-clamped `N*r*`.
