/home/sat/mcrl-v025-floor-ws/CONTROL-LAW-DEMAND-CAPPED-2026-09-10.md:94:The two −2.384185791015625e−7-bit invariant violations are inferred to be floating-operation-order artifacts: the C1 path multiplies `fraction × bandwidth × spectral efficiency`, whereas the C2 replay path forms `bandwidth × spectral efficiency` before multiplying by the fraction. Their size and the passing aggregate parity support that inference, but they are still reported as literal violations and were not rounded away for the proof.
