/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-controller-handoff-20260907/CONTROLLER-REFERENCE-DESIGN-NORMAL-POWER-EE-2026-09-08.md:9:4. **Rate.** ACM maps SINR to a spectral efficiency SE(SINR) from a MODCOD table (DVB-S2X or NR NTN MCS), bounded above by SE_max (≈ 5–6 bit/s/Hz) and below by the lowest MODCOD threshold SINR_min; Shannon-with-gap-and-cap is an acceptable smooth surrogate. Users in a beam share W by TDM (time fractions f_u, Σ f_u ≤ 1) or FDM; equal share is the usual baseline. Per-user rate R_u = f_u·W·SE(SINR_u). Rate follows geometry **every step**; staying on a degrading beam loses bits, not energy.
