    39	I called a sealed rule wrong on the strength of one outside opinion that I had primed by stating my position first. The adversarial review, commissioned to attack me, found the error in under an hour. The lesson is the cheap one: when I am about to overturn a sealed decision, the first step is an adversarial review, not a confirming one.
